BUNDLED GENERATORS — INLINE DEPENDENCIES
========================================

The generators under generators/ each declare their own inline runtime
dependencies via PEP-723 metadata in the entrypoint script's
# /// script header. The generators install these on first run (via uv) —
they do not ship inside the SDK wheel. The complete list across the bundled
generators:

pyyaml
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml

google-genai
  License: Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai

anthropic
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python

docker (docker-py)
  License: Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/docker/docker-py

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BUNDLED RENDERERS — RUNTIME (CDN-LOADED)
========================================

The renderers under renderers/ and builtin/ load their heavy libraries from public CDNs
(https://esm.sh/…, jsdelivr) at runtime rather than vendoring them. The SDK
neither modifies nor redistributes their source. A user-friendly list with
upstream links lives in renderers/CREDITS.md; notable components:

  Monaco Editor          Microsoft                MIT
  Milkdown / Crepe       Milkdown community       MIT
  Excalidraw             Excalidraw Authors       MIT
  Mermaid                Mermaid contributors     MIT
  KaTeX                  KaTeX contributors       MIT
  React, ReactDOM        Facebook / Meta          MIT

See renderers/CREDITS.md for the full list with repository URLs and
manifest entries.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTES ON COMPATIBILITY
======================

All direct and bundled-generator dependencies listed above are permissive
(MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0). The SDK itself is Apache-2.0. No GPL, AGPL, LGPL,
or MPL components are shipped in the wheel. CDN-loaded renderer components
retain their own licenses at the consumer's end — they are not bundled
into the SDK distribution.

